{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra","id":1030886,"title":"Reaching the Deep Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-12T17:46:15-08:00","id":1030886,"title":"Reaching the Deep Umbra","content":"Once of the problems with cWoD is that there seems to be two different Deep Umbras. The Deep Umbra of Mage seems to correspond to the Aetherial Realm of the Near Umbra of Werewolf and the Deep Umbra of Werewolf, but the Deep Umbra of Werewolf also possesses an infinite number of Realms that do not necessarily correspond with the Realms of the Deep Umbra of Mage. I am just curious if everyone thinks that the discrepancy is just caused by the different focuses of the two gamelines or if there are really two different Deep Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:04:50-08:00","id":1030898,"title":"","content":"Something that you knew I'd say: two different Deep Umbrae for two different settings and games that can't be reconciled (on purpose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:25:15-08:00","id":1030913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra#post1030886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once of the problems with cWoD is that there seems to be two different Deep Umbras. The Deep Umbra of Mage seems to correspond to the Aetherial Realm of the Near Umbra of Werewolf and the Deep Umbra of Werewolf, but the Deep Umbra of Werewolf also possesses an infinite number of Realms that do not necessarily correspond with the Realms of the Deep Umbra of Mage. I am just curious if everyone thinks that the discrepancy is just caused by the different focuses of the two gamelines or if there are really two different Deep Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?<br /> <br /> The way I go about it like this. Beyond the Dreamshell, there are three types of &quot;outer space&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's the Aetherian Realm which is described in WTA (and a little bit in the Book of Worlds). There is were the Celestines reside, as well as where you'll find places like Malfeas, Flux, and The Great Machine.<br /> There's Etherspace which is basically the penumbra of space, Here is where you'll find places like Doissetepe, the Seasonal Realms, The Brass City of the Batini, and all of the various Horizon realms.<br /> And Lastly, there's Consensual space, the space the Technocrats tell you about with its cosmic rays, empty vacuums, and the occasional float lump of rock.<br /> Which space you go to depends entirely on your paradigm. If you think space if a vacuum, then it's a vacuum. If you believe it it the realm of the great spirits, then you'll be heading out towards those Celestines. These three iterations of space are as separate as the Penumbra is from the mundane world. To flit between Consensual space and either Etherspace or the Aetherial Reaches would require Spirit 3, but entering the Aetherial Reaches this way is only possible with the spirits allow it, otherwise you're restricted to the former two.<br /> <br /> However, This only applies up until the Horizon, beyond which the differences between these worlds really breaks down and everything starts to become much more melded together. Ether Breathers can Jet alongside Etherships to their left, and Dreamspeaker Spirit Walkers on their right. It is possible to visit the areas described in the Atherial Realms, but again you need the favour of the Celestines to even approach their worlds.<br /> <br /> One way of thinking about this is that the Aetherian Realm, is the Shard Realm of Prime. Each Shard Realm is but a gateway into a completely new galaxy in which one of the nine spheres is the primary building block by which all of physics functions. The S.R. of Matter is a realm in which empty space and matter is inverted, leading to planet sizes pockets of space surrounded by great expanses of earth, metal, and other bits of matter. The S.R. of Life is a great jungle of constantly evolving and shifting lifeforms which spreads out beyond comprehension, while the S.R. of Entropy is where every End of the World scenario resides, and possibly where Vistas come from.<br /> <br /> So yeah. In the umbra, everything exists everywhere right on top of one another, and mage's only limitation in experiencing these places is how willing they are to accept them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:57:26-08:00","id":1030938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1030913#post1030913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not both?<br /> <br /> The way I go about it like this. Beyond the Dreamshell, there are three types of &quot;outer space&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's the Aetherian Realm which is described in WTA (and a little bit in the Book of Worlds). There is were the Celestines reside, as well as where you'll find places like Malfeas, Flux, and The Great Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Celestines actually reside in Werewolf's DU, and Malfeas is also found there outside of Revised (when it became a Near Realm because of the encroaching end times). The planetary spirits of the Aetherial Realm are Incarnae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's Etherspace which is basically the penumbra of space, Here is where you'll find places like Doissetepe, the Seasonal Realms, The Brass City of the Batini, and all of the various Horizon realms. </div> </div> </div>Horizon is a distinctly Mage thing that other monsters don't visit. You'd have the best luck hiding all of the Mage-specific stuff in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Lastly, there's Consensual space, the space the Technocrats tell you about with its cosmic rays, empty vacuums, and the occasional float lump of rock.<br /> Which space you go to depends entirely on your paradigm. If you think space if a vacuum, then it's a vacuum. If you believe it it the realm of the great spirits, then you'll be heading out towards those Celestines. These three iterations of space are as separate as the Penumbra is from the mundane world. To flit between Consensual space and either Etherspace or the Aetherial Reaches would require Spirit 3, but entering the Aetherial Reaches this way is only possible with the spirits allow it, otherwise you're restricted to the former two. </div> </div> </div>Technical issue number two, Werewolf doesn't work by concerns of paradigm or belief. By SAW for W:tA, outer space is physical, the Aetherial Realm is its Penumbral reflection to the point that it's the easiest Near Realm to enter and leave (just step sideways and start flying up), and the Deep Umbra is like another, stranger Penumbra that's physical enough that it doesn't cause disconnection (spirit adaptation, in Mage's lingo). Garou and Fera can travel to all of these. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, This only applies up until the Horizon, beyond which the differences between these worlds really breaks down and everything starts to become much more melded together. Ether Breathers can Jet alongside Etherships to their left, and Dreamspeaker Spirit Walkers on their right. It is possible to visit the areas described in the Atherial Realms, but again you need the favour of the Celestines to even approach their worlds.<br /> <br /> One way of thinking about this is that the Aetherian Realm, is the Shard Realm of Prime. Each Shard Realm is but a gateway into a completely new galaxy in which one of the nine spheres is the primary building block by which all of physics functions. The S.R. of Matter is a realm in which empty space and matter is inverted, leading to planet sizes pockets of space surrounded by great expanses of earth, metal, and other bits of matter. The S.R. of Life is a great jungle of constantly evolving and shifting lifeforms which spreads out beyond comprehension, while the S.R. of Entropy is where every End of the World scenario resides, and possibly where Vistas come from. </div> </div> </div>That's not even remotely what plenatary Incarnae Realms work like in Werewolf, as they're the Penumbral reflections of other planets; Garou and Fera can use Adaptation, step sideways, and end up floating in vacuum, on the moon, standing on Mars, still feeling pretty damned cold on Pluto, floating around in an Oort cloud, etc (and also alive; Adaptation is a key requirement for staying alive during such a jaunt). The only exception is Eshtarra's Realm, which gets weird because it's a werebeast-idealized reflection of Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah. In the umbra, everything exists everywhere right on top of one another, and mage's only limitation in experiencing these places is how willing they are to accept them. </div> </div> </div>Metatext really won't let these settings coexist. To illustrate, to put the above together, you had to break some very foundational assumptions in another game, which is a hard rejection of the other setting. You're not joining the two together in this case, you are filtering another game through Mage. There is no middle ground for their cosmology, and the two games were intentionally designed this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T19:22:43-08:00","id":1030961,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Well yeah... It's a fictional setting. That's what you do. All these rules are exactly what you make of them. And if you decide they don't work at all, then of course they won't.<br /> <br /> If you think Mage is right then Wherewolfs are just as much benders of Consensus as the Mages, but because they are part spirit, they are all sharing the same consensus. So a Werewolf ends up in its part of the Umbra because it believes it will, and its tribe believes it too. If you think Werewolf is right then Mages are some how tapping into Spiritual energy, perhaps the power of a great Celestine or an unseen totem which they explain away as their &quot;Avatar&quot;. They ignorantly shun the spirit world they rely so heavily on for their powers. Perhaps their ancestors even stole their powers from the spirit world, and their difficulty in navigating the Umbra is Gaia's way of limiting their reach, forcing them to stay amongst themselves than unbalance the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it could be argued that there is actually a lot of middleground, it's just the problem is the definitions. Yes, in WTA space has a Penumbra and in MTA it's a bit more involved. Who's to say that this can't occur for both?<br /> <br /> Remember how Mage's experience the Penumbra? One may see the world with the Astral Videre and witness Angels, Celtic Gods, and Epiphlings floating around, while another sees the Videre Spiritum, a world filled with Pattern Spiders, Naturae, and a few Animal Spirits running around, yet one with the Videre Mortem where all around them are the Shadowlands, and world of Wraith.<br /> <br /> Each mage stands in the same place, but see vastly different landscapes with completely different spirits. Even mages with the Astral Videre will see the world differently from one another. Why can't that be the same thing everywhere?<br /> <br /> Mages and Werewolfs experience their two Umbra side by side in the exact way their respective games inform them to, they marvel at who they both seem to experience things so differently but both just chalk it up to the others just being &quot;different&quot;. The Garou consider the Mages intruders, not of the world they explore, and so unable to see it for what it really is.The Mages, on the other hand, say that since the Garou are part spirit, of course they'd experience the spirit world differently from humans.<br /> <br /> There's your middle ground. The idea that the universe doesn't actually work the way either group thinks, but because it works like this when they are amongst their own, they assume it's a universal law.<br /> <br /> Both sides are wrong, but neither one considers this, for it is madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T20:40:29-08:00","id":1030989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1030961#post1030961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Well yeah... It's a fictional setting. That's what you do. All these rules are exactly what you make of them. And if you decide they don't work at all, then of course they won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are fictional settings, and then there are fictional settings purposefully made to mutually annihilate other games when combined with them. Mage and Werewolf are the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think Mage is right then Wherewolfs are just as much benders of Consensus as the Mages, but because they are part spirit, they are all sharing the same consensus. So a Werewolf ends up in its part of the Umbra because it believes it will, and its tribe believes it too. If you think Werewolf is right then Mages are some how tapping into Spiritual energy, perhaps the power of a great Celestine or an unseen totem which they explain away as their &quot;Avatar&quot;. They ignorantly shun the spirit world they rely so heavily on for their powers. Perhaps their ancestors even stole their powers from the spirit world, and their difficulty in navigating the Umbra is Gaia's way of limiting their reach, forcing them to stay amongst themselves than unbalance the spirit world. </div> </div> </div>And that is a very different game from W:tA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, it could be argued that there is actually a lot of middleground, it's just the problem is the definitions. Yes, in WTA space has a Penumbra and in MTA it's a bit more involved. Who's to say that this can't occur for both? </div> </div> </div>Because post-modern hermeticism only works for Mage, and even then maybe not? The other games disagree, sure, but none of them disagrees with each other quite as hard as they disagree with Mage. About the point where M:tA starts asserting that technology is really magick is about the point where other games check out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember how Mage's experience the Penumbra? One may see the world with the Astral Videre and witness Angels, Celtic Gods, and Epiphlings floating around, while another sees the Videre Spiritum, a world filled with Pattern Spiders, Naturae, and a few Animal Spirits running around, yet one with the Videre Mortem where all around them are the Shadowlands, and world of Wraith.<br /> <br /> Each mage stands in the same place, but see vastly different landscapes with completely different spirits. Even mages with the Astral Videre will see the world differently from one another. Why can't that be the same thing everywhere? </div> </div> </div>Because all of the Umbrae are different places, not different visions of the same place. Hence the use of the term step sideways; you're no longer in the exact same place. You are off to the side, in some incomprehensible fashion, beyond the bounds of the physical world, but still in a place that's definitely different from stepping in a different direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages and Werewolfs experience their two Umbra side by side in the exact way their respective games inform them to, they marvel at who they both seem to experience things so differently but both just chalk it up to the others just being &quot;different&quot;. The Garou consider the Mages intruders, not of the world they explore, and so unable to see it for what it really is.The Mages, on the other hand, say that since the Garou are part spirit, of course they'd experience the spirit world differently from humans. </div> </div> </div>Except that Garou and Fera can totally see more of reality than any given mage, in this case, because the changers can go to all of those other places, on account of Werewolf treating them as different, discrete places and not the same reality through a filter. And thus it makes it seem like mages are talking out their asses, because one is living in Demon's restricted cosmology with no Middle Umbra to speak of, and has no idea where the Garou and Fera go when they aren't using the occasional weird rite or high-ranking Beast Courts Gift to get into the land of the dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's your middle ground. The idea that the universe doesn't actually work the way either group thinks, but because it works like this when they are amongst their own, they assume it's a universal law.<br /> <br /> Both sides are wrong, but neither one considers this, for it is madness. </div> </div> </div>No. The side that the group or ST or whoever chooses to be right when playing the game is the one that's right, and the other is wrong. Trying to not choose either means that both end up ramming into each other and exploding into a mess of high energy resentment. Some other details might also be wrong, of course, but those can actually be resolved as mysteries in play. Questions of where Garou go when they step sideways and mages can't find them, because they're in a place that Mage doesn't think exists? Not so conducive to discovery in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T20:52:40-08:00","id":1030994,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Sounds to me like you're quite hell bent on things not working.<br /> And that's fine, if that's how you prefer it. I think it's somewhat limiting.<br /> <br /> All of the umbra is different, true, but it's also constantly shifting. Realms move around, Glens that were side by side yesterday can have a Pattern Web between them tomorrow. It's always shifting, but to a spirit this is normal. Garou are going to have an easier time figuring these changes out than a Mage, especially if they need to think of it like a road map.<br /> <br /> So Garou see more reality, fine. Not a problem. The Umbra is just like that. Mages start on the same path and end up on different sides of the mountain. That Garou have things a bit more consistent because it's their turf. Why is that a problem?<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages seem like they're talking out their asses&quot; Fine. That's how they'd be seen. Not a problem. They have no idea where the Garou go? Again, that's fine. Spirits be crazy doing all sort of stuff humans just don't get. Why should that be game breaking?<br /> <br /> <br /> If you have a Holistic ST, then it's not a problem. It's only a problem if you want it to be a problem.<br /> <br /> Where do the Garou go? That is also a mystery. No one understands the Umbra fully, and there isn't a Mage around who would claim otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-13-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T00:26:19-08:00","id":1031033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1030994#post1030994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do the Garou go? That is also a mystery. No one understands the Umbra fully, and there isn't a Mage around who would claim otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is *one* Mage around who prrrrobably comes damn close, but she is insane, ancient, spent hundreds of years in the Umbra and travels with Black Furies.<br /> <br /> Medea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Or to quote the quote, 'If there is something about the Umbra she does not know, it's probably not worth knowing.'.<br /> But it actually shows what it *takes* to understand the whole thing, so a normal Mage (Or Garou) doesn't even remotely come close, nor a has a chance to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T07:34:12-08:00","id":1031150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1030989#post1030989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there are fictional settings, and then there are fictional settings purposefully made to mutually annihilate other games when combined with them. Mage and Werewolf are the latter.<br /> <br /> No. The side that the group or ST or whoever chooses to be right when playing the game is the one that's right, and the other is wrong. Trying to not choose either means that both end up ramming into each other and exploding into a mess of high energy resentment. Some other details might also be wrong, of course, but those can actually be resolved as mysteries in play. Questions of where Garou go when they step sideways and mages can't find them, because they're in a place that Mage doesn't think exists? Not so conducive to discovery in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying they are 'purposefully made to mutually annihilate other games' is a massive exaggeration. And high energy resentment will only occur if you have immature players who need to wag on how their game line is better. I'm no umbral expert, so I won't really get into how incompatible one or the other is. But I think this point might be overstated as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:30:13-08:00","id":1031168,"title":"","content":"Well, CtD, KotE, VtM, and WtO players really do not care about the argument of which Deep Umbra is correct (while they deal with the Umbra, they rarely deal with the Deep Umbra), so the argument is really between MtAs and WtA. MtAs focuses on the subjective nature of the interpretations of Mages, as their perceptions of are filtered through their avatars and their paradigms, so their perspective is unreliable by design. Since WtA focuses on creatures who are half-spirit and are practically native to the Umbra (in the case of the Corax, the Garou, and the Nuwisha), the perspective of Fera are considered to be objective (every Fera tends to see the same thing when they meet the same spirit, though they will react differently based on culture indoctrination and personal experience). <br /> <br /> So, the question then becomes one of subjectivity over objectivity? Do you trust the group that gleefully embraces subjective perceptions in order to explain differences in perception and just think the Fera to share the same paradigm? Or do you trust the group with the shared perception, despite the diversity of its membership, that considers the other group to be a bunch of lunatics cracking under the strain of Umbral perception? If you prefer MtAs, you will go with subjectivity. If you prefer WtA, you will go with objectivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:14:47-08:00","id":1033139,"title":"","content":"A guy saying that the shapeshifters, creatures BOND by their roles and natures, know more than mages that are BOUNDLESS and BEND THE VERY REALLITY.<br /> <br /> Yep, sure.<br /> <br /> But again, what could be expected from a WTA player fanatical...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:21:45-08:00","id":1033141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033139#post1033139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A guy saying that the shapeshifters, creatures BOND by their roles and natures, know more than mages that are BOUNDLESS and BEND THE VERY REALLITY.<br /> <br /> Yep, sure.<br /> <br /> But again, what could be expected from a WTA player fanatical...</div> </div> </div> </div>I already laid out the reasoning for that; by the book, the Mage part doesn't even view itself as boundless in how it describes videres. They're limited in this game of alleged limitlessness, whereas the perspective of other games (not just Werewolf, mind you; Wraith, Changeling and KotE also get in on this) only ever leaves out Horizon, and Vampire and Demon only leave out the Middle Umbra and Horizon. Furthermore, mages only visit one Deep Umbra or space, whereas the other games go through the Deep Umbra, space, and the Aetherial Realm. Shall I <i>reiterate</i> this <i>x</i> number of times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T21:46:20-08:00","id":1033144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033139#post1033139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A guy saying that the shapeshifters, creatures BOND by their roles and natures, know more than mages that are BOUNDLESS and BEND THE VERY REALLITY.<br /> <br /> Yep, sure.<br /> <br /> But again, what could be expected from a WTA player fanatical...</div> </div> </div> </div>So not to be overly critical, but your statements (to me) come off as extremely condescending and (to echo you) incredibly Mage fanatical.<br /> <br /> That being said, I actually think Mages are probably the least reliable sources for information since each and every one of them have to view reality through their own biased viewpoint. Anything printed in a Mage book that is information given in-character is almost certainly skewed of false to some degree.<br /> <br /> Also, OOC the Mage books give a great deal on helpful information about various Umbral locations. That same information can sometimes conflict with the OOC information given in Werewolf books, the other main source of information we have on the Umbras. When you have incompatible OOC information from various books, it's left up to individual STs to decide how the cosmology lines up. Both <i>can't</i> be right. This isn't an insurmountable problem by any means, but it does take the ST deciding for themselves which line to take primarily from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T22:18:04-08:00","id":1033157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033139#post1033139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A guy saying that the shapeshifters, creatures BOND by their roles and natures, know more than mages that are BOUNDLESS and BEND THE VERY REALLITY.<br /> <br /> Yep, sure.<br /> <br /> But again, what could be expected from a WTA player fanatical...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to fall in your back, but the fact that mages bend the reality isn't exactly helping your argument.<br /> A mage can choose to be right, he never has to be wrong again. Until Paradox strikes.<br /> Hybris and the temptation of power are both important themes.<br /> If Mage is right, then there's no objective truth, (unless All are united under the same or at least similar Paradigm) All are right in their respective zone.<br /> If the Garou are right, Mage isn't right either.<br /> BTW<br /> If I had to choose one game before the other, then it would be mage. You could even call me fanatical...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:07:46-08:00","id":1033393,"title":"","content":"Can someone please state what the main contradiction between OOC Mage and OOC Werewolf is regarding the umbra, because I still don't see how the Aetharian Realm, the Mundane Space, and Etherspace can't coincide with one another. Layered on top of one another with Werewolfs having the greatest amount of control over which one they witness, while Mages are fairly stuck in which ever they believe they are in.<br /> <br /> Because as far as I can tell, all forms of Umbra are correct, and infact there may two dramatically overlapping umbrae lining the entire universe. If a werewolf and a mage walk the same way, either they will be seperated as the paths get murky, or they will enter parts of the overlap where either part can be correct as they flakes away into one or the other.<br /> <br /> The Mages may visit the True Umbra. but the Werewolves live in the Real Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:25:46-08:00","id":1033438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can someone please state what the main contradiction between OOC Mage and OOC Werewolf is regarding the umbra, because I still don't see how the Aetharian Realm, the Mundane Space, and Etherspace can't coincide with one another. Layered on top of one another with Werewolfs having the greatest amount of control over which one they witness, while Mages are fairly stuck in which ever they believe they are in. </div> </div> </div>Well, in the Book of Worlds, things were like that. Then the authors started changing stuff. For instance, according to VE Convention Book, Mundane Space reaches up to the Asteroid Belt, after that, there's no &quot;material&quot; space.<br /> Since the authors don't fell compelled to make things coherent between lines, you cannot say that they're both correct without making judgements of your own about these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:35:41-08:00","id":1033450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033438#post1033438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in the Book of Worlds, things were like that. Then the authors started changing stuff. For instance, according to VE Convention Book, Mundane Space reaches up to the Asteroid Belt, after that, there's no &quot;material&quot; space.<br /> Since the authors don't fell compelled to make things coherent between lines, you cannot say that they're both correct without making judgements of your own about these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's how the Deep Umbra works for the Void Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:38:53-08:00","id":1033452,"title":"","content":"Yes, in Werewolf, Outer Space is Outer Space, regardless of how far out you are. You could go to the Aetherial Realm of Pluto, cross into the Deep Umbra Realm of Pluto through the Anchorhead, and then step sideways onto the material surface of Pluto (though that is a one-way trip for most Garou if they lack the appropriate Gifts). Within Mage, Mages do not seem to accept the physical existence of Outer Space beyond the Main Belt, so they are incapable of crossing from the Deep Umbra to Outer Space beyond the Main Belt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:41:21-08:00","id":1033454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033450#post1033450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that's how the Deep Umbra works for the Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf states that that isn't how the Umbra works. So you can do that, but you are choosing to use Mage primarily over Werewolf, which is kind of the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:58:40-08:00","id":1033469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033454#post1033454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf states that that isn't how the Umbra works. So you can do that, but you are choosing to use Mage primarily over Werewolf, which is kind of the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how Werewolf states the deep umbra works is how the deep umbra works for Werewolves. What's the problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:53:01-08:00","id":1033512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not?<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's how the Deep Umbra works for the Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Exactly.</b><br /> <br /> That &quot;perhaps&quot; it's where you slam your judgement. There's no &quot;perhaps&quot; in the VE book, much less in the Werewolf bibliography. That &quot;perhaps&quot; belogs to a mentality born with the Book of Worlds and a Traditionalist view of the Umbra. When you make that &quot;perhaps&quot; to be the way things works, you've already opted for a methaphysic (a relativistic one).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:58:30-08:00","id":1033519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033512#post1033512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Exactly.</b><br /> <br /> That &quot;perhaps&quot; it's where you slam your judgement. There's no &quot;perhaps&quot; in the VE book, much less in the Werewolf bibliography. That &quot;perhaps&quot; belogs to a mentality born with the Book of Worlds and a Traditionalist view of the Umbra. When you make that &quot;perhaps&quot; to be the way things works, you've already opted for a methaphysic (a relativistic one).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so if I were to say authoritatively that that is how it works for VE's, there wouldn't be a problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:25:40-08:00","id":1033544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, so if I were to say authoritatively that that is how it works for VE's, there wouldn't be a problem? </div> </div> </div>Then you would be imposing Revised Infinite Tapestry/VE Convention Book Mage canon (instead of a relativistic homemade solution that's somewhat like the one in Book of Worlds) to the werewolves. Neither respects how werewolves see the Umbra. Neither it's a &quot;solution&quot; of the contradictions, because neither respects the way both mage and werewolf see this stuff. Both can be a &quot;solution&quot; (in another sense) because ST has the final word on metaphysics. Passing a judgement isn't wrong (it's the Storyteller's job), but know that you're doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:31:44-08:00","id":1033549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033544#post1033544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you would be imposing Revised Infinite Tapestry/VE Convention Book Mage canon (instead of a relativistic homemade solution that's somewhat like the one in Book of Worlds) to the werewolves. Neither respects how werewolves see the Umbra. Neither it's a &quot;solution&quot; of the contradictions, because neither respects the way both mage and werewolf see this stuff. Both can be a &quot;solution&quot; (in another sense) because ST has the final word on metaphysics. Passing a judgement isn't wrong (it's the Storyteller's job), but know that you're doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps the Umbra is much more fluid than this. It could be the Revised era Umbra is how it is one week, then the next week it shifts. It could be that the VE interpretation of the umbra is completely true so long as you are in a ship travleing around. It could be that the Aetherian Realm only works if you travel across it from the start.<br /> <br /> So why not have WTA be consistent and MTA fluctuate depending on who happens to be in the room at the time? Why create an Either/Or scenario for something which literally defies conventional understanding? Why deny a holistic approach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:18:09-08:00","id":1033587,"title":"","content":"It is much more likely that the Werewolves, who are effectively native to the Umbra, are capable of seeing 'reality' than the Mages, who are effectively foreign to the Umbra. Mages do not have the natural senses to perceive the Umbra, so they have to filter their perceptions through their Avatars and their Paradigms. The fact that Werewolves can visit the Aetherial and Physical versions of Pluto while the Mages can only visit the Deep Umbra versions of Pluto suggests that the Werewolves have more options when it comes to the Middle and Deep Umbra than Mages. Heck, Mages do not even mention the Aetherial Realm when they discuss the Middle Umbra, so they might not even be allowed into the Aetherial Realm by Spirits of the Middle Umbra. Oh, by the way, the Werewolves are aware of the Horizon, they just call it the Membrane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:28:40-08:00","id":1033597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033587#post1033587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is much more likely that the Werewolves, who are effectively native to the Umbra, are capable of seeing 'reality' than the Mages, who are effectively foreign to the Umbra. Mages do not have the natural senses to perceive the Umbra, so they have to filter their perceptions through their Avatars and their Paradigms. The fact that Werewolves can visit the Aetherial and Physical versions of Pluto while the Mages can only visit the Deep Umbra versions of Pluto suggests that the Werewolves have more options when it comes to the Middle and Deep Umbra than Mages. Heck, Mages do not even mention the Aetherial Realm when they discuss the Middle Umbra, so they might not even be allowed into the Aetherial Realm by Spirits of the Middle Umbra. Oh, by the way, the Werewolves are aware of the Horizon, they just call it the Membrane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible for a mage to visit the Aetherial Realm, but they would only be able to do it from the ground up. No constant shifting from mundane space to Aetherial space for them.They'd have to start from the Middle Umbra, not be a Technomancer (really important, that one), have a good reputation with a number of spirits, and then proceed to fly/walk their way beyond the stars.<br /> <br /> For the Mage, they would be in a separate place from &quot;Etherspace&quot; until the Horizon, after which anything can happen. Their Aetherial walk can bleed into a Void Engineers vessel and the void that it passes through, as well as a number of other realms which can just bounce about up there.<br /> One minute they might be walking across an empty cosmic desert, the next an Ethership with a Astronautic Etherite would be floating by them trying to get them to come aboard.<br /> <br /> The Werewolf, on the other hand, would be able to shift between these various kinds of Umbra on a whim. There is much less drifitng, and much more choice on how they would approach things in the umbra, because to them it's a simple matter of stepping sideways.<br /> <br /> What would the Mage see if they were watching this? Honestly they would have no idea, first there werewolf would be there, then it wouldn't, then it would but in a different place. Then maybe somewhere completely different. If it was a Void Engineer, they might not even see the werewolf at all unless it boarded their vessel and sidestepped into mundane space.<br /> <br /> I guess the basic question to &quot;Which umbra are we in?&quot; at this point is simply &quot;yes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:45:59-08:00","id":1033612,"title":"","content":"Mage perspective is subjective. And the Technocratic view is even more narrowed. For instance, the Union forbade any knews about Ceres, the tiny moon of Mercury. The reason of that, probably is because it were hold by the Traditions (in the meta plot, the Union attacked that Traditionalist stronghold, only to lose it almost immediatly for a large Nephandi force). So, to the Consensus, that moon simply doesn't exist... No mundane telescope will ever see it.<br /> <br /> So, the time table of the VE says &quot;go with easy... Lets normatize one section out a time... For now, leave everything beyond the asteroid belt for another time&quot;. Just because the VE said this, doesn't mean it is right. It certanly isn't for the Traditions! The VE also say that &quot;spirit&quot; is a mambo jambo of superstitious backwards people; those things are simply &quot;transdimensional entities&quot; or the likes of it. Hell, not even ALL VE will believe this! Certanly, members of the Control will have the &quot;greater truth&quot; in their tables. For example: the Masters know ghosts are real. But to the Low ranked non awakened agent, the truth is very simple: ghosts are bullshit. Illusions. That's the truth. Control said so itself, period.<br /> <br /> Why holding the VE view to be considered as the ultimate truth? (unless you're a Technocrat, that doesn't even make any sense, and if you are a Technocrat but doesn't agree with this... Fake it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:52:21-08:00","id":1033617,"title":"","content":"Maybe in 10 years from now, their time table will move to include all solar system, in 100 up to Alpha Centaury, in 1000 the hole galaxy.<br /> <br /> And it's funny that VE book says that, and in the meanwhile they keep feeding to the masses the Consensus of outer space stars and planets outside the solar system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:53:37-08:00","id":1033618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033549#post1033549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or perhaps the Umbra is much more fluid than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage, with Mage alone as the game, it is. It's the only game to actually state that this situation is the order of the day, the odd duck out among the WoD, so if you do say that the Umbra is really fluid and shows up differently to different observers, you're only going by the way that Mage works. Even if you try to say that the Umbra works differently for other monsters, it's still the way that Mage does things above the way that other games figure things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be the Revised era Umbra is how it is one week, then the next week it shifts. It could be that the VE interpretation of the umbra is completely true so long as you are in a ship travleing around. It could be that the Aetherian Realm only works if you travel across it from the start.<br /> <br /> So why not have WTA be consistent and MTA fluctuate depending on who happens to be in the room at the time? Why create an Either/Or scenario for something which literally defies conventional understanding? Why deny a holistic approach? </div> </div> </div>Because it's not the way that the cosmologies of other games work. The Dark Umbra is different from the Middle and the Astral and the Deep, all of which admit entry in very different ways and occupy different spiritual spaces, often with denizens that observe wholly different mechanical systems. That's why The Thousand Hells, which blend together the lands of living and dead spirits, are unique. That's how the other games gain focus and don't step on others' toes. That's how the other games gain particular flavors of their own that make them feel distinct from each other.<br /> <br /> There's no defiance of conventional understanding. While all the games have the makings of occupying parallel universes with only a few vague similarities and loosely shared events, Mage's parallel universe line is just further away from the others than all of the others are from each other, and there's far less blurring together with it and other lines. Moving it closer together would be a rather trying, if not impossible, effort, provided you wanted to keep Mage as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:19:18-08:00","id":1033636,"title":"","content":"Every perspective is subjective.<br /> Neither side could possibly coerce the other side, because both sides have direct personal evidence/witnessed their true reality.<br /> <br /> If it is so important to some of you, then go and make the WtA view the only true and right one.<br /> <br /> Mages tend to not care for such small things like what OTHERS think its real after all...<br /> <br /> Changing the Umbrae wouldn't really make any difference. At most you have to explain why suddenly mages in deep umbran travel function like Marauders, in the sense that they take their reality with them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:23:05-08:00","id":1033642,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> See, here's the main problem I have with your conceit. You're taking the view that middleground cannot exist because middleground existing = Mage. Werewolf says it's like this, therefore any attempt to deviate from what Werewolf states is Mage.<br /> It's a really narrow way of viewing things, and closes the door to any kind of extrapolation, interpretation, or reexamining.<br /> <br /> Also, what are you talking about regarding the other cosmologies? Wraith takes place almost exclusively in the Dark Umbra, their penumbra, the Shadowlands, is basically the Videre Mortum, but they are unable to communicate with the spirits because they can only see the living or the dead, not the spiritual. In order for a mage to interact with the shadowlands properly, they must either go through the Agatham Sojourn or die. They can cross the gauntlet and gimpse at the Shadowlands, but crossing the Veil to walk around there is a different matter.<br /> <br /> After that point, things are basically like they are in WTO, Nihils to get to the Tempest, Walk around Stygia, get drowned into a Harrowing, fend of Spectres in the Labyrinth, all the while being attacked by any wraith who doesn't like who alive you happen to be. Werewolves can visit the deadlands too, but usually don't have much cause to do so. There are theories that the Wyrm and Oblivion share a strange relationship, and that while one pushes forward for corruption, the other slowly pulls. It may even be the case that after the apocalypse, the Wyrm may plunge itself into Oblivion, thereby unmaking itself in its final act, returning all to nothing.<br /> <br /> The Astral Umbra is basically its own thing, but Werewolves are able to visit if they tried. It just makes absolutely no sense to them. There is reason to say that the Far Shores of the lower umbra are connected to the Afterworlds of the Astral Realm. Where concepts of the underworld and the memories and passions embodied may intermingle. It may even be possible for a Wraith to escape the afterworlds and find themselves in the astral realm proper. Though such a journey is likely to be fraught with peril and may even be impossible for most. Alternatively this could be where the thoughts of Wraiths who transcend end up, making up the fabric of the astral realm, from the Vulgate to the Epiphamies.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget the Dreaming though. The Dreaming probably has the most overlap with the Middle Umbra, but it is possible to approach both the Astral and Dark umbra is one was so inclined to do so.<br /> <br /> You might say &quot;It doesn't work like that&quot;. I say it can totally work like that. Then you say &quot;Only if every game is Mage&quot; to which I say every game is WoD, it's just that Mages get to go everywhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> You don't want it to work. That's why it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:12:22-08:00","id":1033814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033642#post1033642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> See, here's the main problem I have with your conceit. You're taking the view that middleground cannot exist because middleground existing = Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a rather steep slope, given how all-encompassing Mage tries to be. Not that any games have to go with it, of course, and since they have their own structures and wildly divergent themes that often aren't helped by Mage's POV on cosmology, it tends to be a cascade problem from even a tiny change. For instance, take Mage's claim that all humans have awakened avatars that are sleeping, but are otherwise potential Awakened. This setup wouldn't really allow the assumption of where the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen get their Imbued, since they never choose any humans that are tied to existing powers for empowering as Reckoning hunters, and having an avatar, even if it is asleep, would tend to tie one to being a Mage pretty heavily..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf says it's like this, therefore any attempt to deviate from what Werewolf states is Mage. </div> </div> </div>As I've noted, it's not actually just Werewolf. Wraith went in another direction, and so did Changeling (relating to both the Dreaming as a separate thing and the structure of ghosts being in what the Nunnehi called the Lower World and living spirits being in the Higher World), and then Wraith started doing a lot of lifting for KotE and Mummy. At this point, Werewolf is just part of the stream that Mage is swimming against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a really narrow way of viewing things, and closes the door to any kind of extrapolation, interpretation, or reexamining. </div> </div> </div>But with the Umbrae having a known structure, it gives places where it can actually deviate. Again, places like the Thousand Hells. I'm honestly not seeing anything to gain from the subjectivity of videres, given that. It just seems to kill any impetus to actually explore, if everything is defined by the outlook.<br /> <br /> Which, again, is a major part of Mage, but isn't really present in other games. In the Penumbra, a Garou that walks a given distance and then steps sideways again ends up in a point that given distance from the corresponding point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what are you talking about regarding the other cosmologies? Wraith takes place almost exclusively in the Dark Umbra, their penumbra, the Shadowlands, is basically the Videre Mortum, but they are unable to communicate with the spirits because they can only see the living or the dead, not the spiritual. </div> </div> </div>Except that it has many different paradigms of death by culture, and is also linked into other games (KotE and Mummy), which goes against the proposed structure of Mage. Also, it never suggests that outer space is a spirit world and not a physical one, or that technology is magic(k).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Astral Umbra is basically its own thing, but Werewolves are able to visit if they tried. It just makes absolutely no sense to them. There is reason to say that the Far Shores of the lower umbra are connected to the Afterworlds of the Astral Realm. Where concepts of the underworld and the memories and passions embodied may intermingle. It may even be possible for a Wraith to escape the afterworlds and find themselves in the astral realm proper. Though such a journey is likely to be fraught with peril and may even be impossible for most. Alternatively this could be where the thoughts of Wraiths who transcend end up, making up the fabric of the astral realm, from the Vulgate to the Epiphamies. </div> </div> </div>Fun story about the Astral Umbra, it used to be a sub-section in the Werewolf Deep Umbra. There's a sidebar in the Mokole book outlining how the setup in 2e Werewolf and 2e Mage differed, in fact. Werewolf Deep and Astral Umbrae didn't get shifted to even kind of line up with Mage until W20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's not forget the Dreaming though. The Dreaming probably has the most overlap with the Middle Umbra, but it is possible to approach both the Astral and Dark umbra is one was so inclined to do so. </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming, though, is still its own thing, no matter where passages to various Umbrae might end up. Other Umbrae have more definite passages where one might open up into another; those aren't really news, though, since things like shallowings and hellholes have been around for a long time and still rely on an otherwise keen separation between different Umbrae..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might say &quot;It doesn't work like that&quot;. I say it can totally work like that. Then you say &quot;Only if every game is Mage&quot; to which I say every game is WoD, it's just that Mages get to go everywhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> You don't want it to work. That's why it doesn't. </div> </div> </div>I only really got attached to the notion that they don't go together very well because it was expressed by people who worked on the game, and I was bitter about my old group always slamming shit together whichever way. Had I not heard the breathtaking notion that Mage didn't dictate what the entire thing was actually like, I wouldn't be feeling the need to correct what seems by all rights to be a factual error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:23:05-08:00","id":1033825,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Honestly, it just seems like you're trying to argue that it's wrong to consider a tomato as a vegetable. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmxIK9p0SNM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmxIK9p0SNM</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:25:48-08:00","id":1033828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033825#post1033825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Honestly, it just seems like you're trying to argue that it's wrong to consider a tomato as a vegetable. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmxIK9p0SNM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XmxIK9p0SNM</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Should I go for the bait...<br /> <br /> Ah, hell, why not. It's a fruit because it has seeds in it. That's how you can tell it was a plant ovary.<br /> <br /> I suppose that makes this post one that... (sunglasses on) picks the low-hanging fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:30:04-08:00","id":1033834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033828#post1033828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should I go for the bait...<br /> <br /> Ah, hell, why not. It's a fruit because it has seeds in it. That's how you can tell it was a plant ovary.<br /> <br /> I suppose that makes this post one that... (sunglasses on) picks the low-hanging fruit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, now watch the video and see why such a point of view is irrelevant and unhelpful when regarding purely subjective matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:38:44-08:00","id":1033835,"title":"","content":"It is a fruit because it is a fruit of a plant (it arises from a blossom and exists to provide nutrition for the seed). Vegetables are bulbs, flowers, leaves, roots, or stems of plants. Fruits and nuts are the bodies that are created by plants to nourish the seeds.<br /> <br /> If you want to use that analogy though, we will. In Werewolf, a tomato is a fruit because it serves the function of a fruit because Werewolves see the reality of the tomato plant and, when a Werewolf talks about tomato spirits, they are talking about the Gaian spirit associated with the tomato plant. In Mage, however, a tomato is an appetizer, a fruit, a salad, a sandwich, a vegetable, and everything in between because Mages see every concept of the tomato plant rather of the reality tomato plant and, when a Mage talks about tomato spirits, they could be talking about anything from the Lord of Ketchup in the High Umbra to the Wraith of Hernan Cortes, the conquistador who brought the first tomato plants to Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:54:02-08:00","id":1033844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033835#post1033835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a fruit because it is a fruit of a plant (it arises from a blossom and exists to provide nutrition for the seed). Vegetables are bulbs, flowers, leaves, roots, or stems of plants. Fruits and nuts are the bodies that are created by plants to nourish the seeds.<br /> <br /> If you want to use that analogy though, we will. In Werewolf, a tomato is a fruit because it serves the function of a fruit because Werewolves see the reality of the tomato plant and, when a Werewolf talks about tomato spirits, they are talking about the Gaian spirit associated with the tomato plant. In Mage, however, a tomato is an appetizer, a fruit, a salad, a sandwich, a vegetable, and everything in between because Mages see every concept of the tomato plant rather of the reality tomato plant and, when a Mage talks about tomato spirits, they could be talking about anything from the Lord of Ketchup in the High Umbra to the Wraith of Hernan Cortes, the conquistador who brought the first tomato plants to Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This tangent seems silly, but that second paragraph was worth a good laugh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T04:00:34-08:00","id":1033944,"title":"","content":"Now I know whom to ask the big meaningful questions: the Big Furry Ones.<br /> You convinced me, obviously the Garou see the reality as it truly is. They don't have any problems regarding phenomenalism or other crap that puzzles philosophers for thousands of years.<br /> Oh wait, they possibly know about tomato spirits because they are half-plants themselves.<br /> <br /> The first big question I should ask:<br /> Are they fruits or vegetables?<br /> <br /> Ritual Disclaimer for the short fused Forumites:<br /> Do not take this post too serious.<br /> Think before posting.<br /> Don't assume the worst possible meaning.<br /> Have fun!<br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T05:34:24-08:00","id":1033968,"title":"","content":"I probably should be annoyed the point I was trying to make has been so thiroughly lost, but screw it, werewolfs are now tomatoes. I can live with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:36:42-08:00","id":1033983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why not have WTA be consistent and MTA fluctuate depending on who happens to be in the room at the time? Why create an Either/Or scenario for something which literally defies conventional understanding? Why deny a holistic approach?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your decision to make. Nothing of what's written in werewolf can be interpreted this way without adding mages to the mix, and thus, this this it's YOUR headcanon about how a crossover WoD would work. This it's more <i>diplomatic</i>, but no less of an imposition on your part, than saying that VE are right. MY own headcanon can be different, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:20:50-08:00","id":1033992,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> So, let's move on to something more interesting. If we accept that the umbra is a completely different entity for each gameline, and crossovers either need to compromise or use a less well defined umbra in order to work. What then are we saying about a MTA WTA crossover?<br /> <br /> It's been declared several times that such crossovers would simply be werewolves running around in a MTA game. So how would the opposite work? Mages running around a WTA game.<br /> <br /> Would it simply be the mage is treated like a generic mystic/shaman/scientist/what have you without concentrating so much on how they do their magic, but rather on how it affects the world and in turn Gaia?<br /> Would they be able to go pretty much anywhere the Werewolves are capable of going in the plot demands it?<br /> Is there no distinction between the three umbrae, and the Dark Umbra and Astral Umbra are just either non-existant or make up a very niche part of the main umbra?<br /> <br /> If running a Werewolf game, is there any value in using the holistic model of the Umbra whenever a Mage shows up?<br /> If running a Mage game, does the umbra lose anything if running the Werewolf model?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:30:39-08:00","id":1033997,"title":"","content":"Mage in a Werewolves game has to play with a WtA Umbra. This mage should get in touch with his spiritual/animal side and avoid drawing spotlight to mage-themes.<br /> <br /> Garou in a Mage game should be equally mindful of proper etiquette and be aware of the fact, that they are not in Kansas anymore (the Umbra could be rather strange).<br /> <br /> In Essence:<br /> Crossovers are not so much of a Problem if the minority can deal with the fact that the majority sets up the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:40:22-08:00","id":1034004,"title":"","content":"Well, the Garou would probably think that the Mages were insane after the first couple of trips to the Umbra and would likely avoid traveling to the Umbra with their Mage friends to avoid too much confusion. The exception may be Dreamspeakers and Verbena who share a Gaian paradigm, as they might interpret things close enough to the Garou that the Garou might not think they were insane. The fact that Mages are vulnerable to the Avatar Storm also means that the Garou may want to save their friends from the pain associated from having their souls shredded as well.<br /> <br /> One problem that Mages have in a crossover is that they find it difficult to keep up with Garou in physical combat and the Umbra. Mages cannot regenerate damage as easily as Garou do, and they do not naturally soak lethal or aggravated damage. Even a relatively weak combat Fomori will be able to kill a combat expert Mage, so Mages really need to leave the fighting to the Garou. <br /> <br /> The utility of Mages to their Garou allies is in their flexibility, not their power, and one Mage can provide support equivalent to dozens of Kinfolk for their Gaoru allies. Mages end up dealing with normal humans, spying on Pentex locations, negotiating for them with the local Kindred, etc. A Garou group supported by a couple of properly designed Mages will likely be much more effective than a Garou group supported by a couple dozen Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:15:54-08:00","id":1034103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034004#post1034004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Garou would probably think that the Mages were insane after the first couple of trips to the Umbra and would likely avoid traveling to the Umbra with their Mage friends to avoid too much confusion. The exception may be Dreamspeakers and Verbena who share a Gaian paradigm, as they might interpret things close enough to the Garou that the Garou might not think they were insane. The fact that Mages are vulnerable to the Avatar Storm also means that the Garou may want to save their friends from the pain associated from having their souls shredded as well.<br /> <br /> One problem that Mages have in a crossover is that they find it difficult to keep up with Garou in physical combat and the Umbra. Mages cannot regenerate damage as easily as Garou do, and they do not naturally soak lethal or aggravated damage. Even a relatively weak combat Fomori will be able to kill a combat expert Mage, so Mages really need to leave the fighting to the Garou. <br /> <br /> The utility of Mages to their Garou allies is in their flexibility, not their power, and one Mage can provide support equivalent to dozens of Kinfolk for their Gaoru allies. Mages end up dealing with normal humans, spying on Pentex locations, negotiating for them with the local Kindred, etc. A Garou group supported by a couple of properly designed Mages will likely be much more effective than a Garou group supported by a couple dozen Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the most simplistic view I could ever think about a Mage... To equalize one to mere normal humans... &quot;A little more useful human&quot;. Damn. I'm sure you don't play Mage AT ALL.<br /> <br /> Yes, Mages are not killing machines like the shapeshifters. But to say something roughly as &quot;one Mage equals 6 kinfolk in usefulness&quot; is to be totally oblivious about the capabilities of Mages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:25:03-08:00","id":1034108,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> That was uncalled for, and also really unhelpful.<br /> <br /> Anyway, While it's good to know about the relative strengths and weaknesses between the two groups. I'm not asking for this.<br /> I'm more interested in comparing the various models on the umbra, and how they function when used with characters outside of the game line they were intended for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:42:33-08:00","id":1034111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's move on to something more interesting. If we accept that the umbra is a completely different entity for each gameline, and crossovers either need to compromise or use a less well defined umbra in order to work. What then are we saying about a MTA WTA crossover?<br /> <br /> It's been declared several times that such crossovers would simply be werewolves running around in a MTA game. So how would the opposite work? Mages running around a WTA game.<br /> <br /> Would it simply be the mage is treated like a generic mystic/shaman/scientist/what have you without concentrating so much on how they do their magic, but rather on how it affects the world and in turn Gaia?<br /> Would they be able to go pretty much anywhere the Werewolves are capable of going in the plot demands it?<br /> Is there no distinction between the three umbrae, and the Dark Umbra and Astral Umbra are just either non-existant or make up a very niche part of the main umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you use Werewolf books. There are strong distinctions between the Three Umbrae, perhaps more than in Mage, as there's no interrelated Videres sharing a Penumbral landscape.<br /> <br /> Mages are reality warpers that reshape reality like they were powerful spirits (Paradigms are mere delusions). They may be an abomination to Gaia (or perhaps this it's a werewolf prejudice, it wouldn't be the first).<br /> <br /> Mages may not be able to go wherever werewolves go, but not because their perception of reality doesn't encompass that particular Umbral manifestation, but because they're forbidden by the spirits to go to that place, or because they lack the powers needed to travel there. A subtle but powerful difference, that may impede your Gaian Dreamspeaker from going to garou sacred lands, despite being paradigmatically OK for him.<br /> <br /> Certain places where mages go might not exist, or maybe they exist but are interpreted in a &quot;werewolf way&quot;. This may be as simple or as hard as you want.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers can now explore very far in conventional space, indeed, now that material space encompases all the universe. They should be very happy with this, as they're not inventing the void and setting the laws of physics while they travel, they were already set from the begining-this it's a stronger confirmation of a scientific world than the Antrophic Principle. Too bad that they're unwitting pawns of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:45:46-08:00","id":1034112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1033944#post1033944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I know whom to ask the big meaningful questions: the Big Furry Ones.<br /> You convinced me, obviously the Garou see the reality as it truly is. They don't have any problems regarding phenomenalism or other crap that puzzles philosophers for thousands of years.<br /> Oh wait, they possibly know about tomato spirits because they are half-plants themselves.<br /> <br /> The first big question I should ask:<br /> Are they fruits or vegetables?<br /> <br /> Ritual Disclaimer for the short fused Forumites:<br /> Do not take this post too serious.<br /> Think before posting.<br /> Don't assume the worst possible meaning.<br /> Have fun!<br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I've always felt about WtA &quot;entusiasthics&quot;, and the disciples of the cult of the Wolf always bothered me for being like that... They believe their precious game is the best work of fiction ever, and that their game is the most genious thing ever made since the fire, and all the rest are second class citizens unworth of note, and dare you not to defy their holy scripture that contains all the universal truths written in stone.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I think theirs is a silly game about bulldogs on steroids that go on to be the ecological correct group of the WoD, trying to save the world while living in the woods and interbreeding amongst cosins, a game of &quot;cowboy vs indians&quot;, with no real deapth, no real personal horror, no real great questioning. In WtA, you're either on the team of Gaia, or you're a villain. Unlike Vampire, were no matter if you're Sabbat or Camarilla, you're probably an anti hero, or in changelling were you can be a hero or anti hero and still having the dictomy of Seelie vs Unseelie, and all the struggle of hope vs despair, or in Mage were you can be a hero no matter if under the Traditions or the Union, and may even recognize the worthness of your opponent but still remain a bitter enemy, or in wraith were you struggle with yourself... In werewolf, there is nothing of that. It's quite simple: if Gaia dies, everybody loses. So, what can we do? Fight. Period. That's it.<br /> <br /> Tell me, why would any Garou be seduced by the Wyrm, unless he is ignorant about the Garou society or mad? Only an idiot would do that. In fact, &quot;seduction by Wyrm&quot; is not even a theme i wta. Why is a black spiral dancer &quot;of the wyrm&quot;? Simple: he were born by the wrong parents. Why the other Garou are Champions of Gaia? Simple, they had the RIGHT parents.<br /> <br /> Now, in Mage, there is a very real promisse of power. Power for a werewolf isn't that important after all... What would a Garou aspire for? Rank 5? Leadership of a Pack, or a Caern? Well, those are social stances, and doesn't leave much room for alien ancients to make Machiavellian agreements for REAL power to the individual that are one of the essences of the Nefandi Descent. Shifters don't have the inner struggle that endangers their very sense of the self, that is the essence of the themes of Nefandi AND marauders in mage, or the excepcional struggle of a wraith against itself, incarnated in the image of the spectres, or the struggle for balance that a changelling needs to keep the banality in check or to avoid the dissolution of the Ego in the chaos of Bedlam, losing oneself to its own fantasies. And, if you wanna play a higly political conspiracy game, Vampire is thousands times more complex.<br /> <br /> And yet, werewolf players deal with WtA as the Gaia's holy words, and anyone that disagrees is an heretic in the eyes of their Goddess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:18:55-08:00","id":1034130,"title":"","content":"I would be comfortable enough with WtA for a PC choosing a Garou over a Mage in one of my Mage games, but I would not attempt to ST anything WtA-centric over in scope than an One-Shot.<br /> Naturally this leads to my standard warning for the Crossover PC: &quot;Don't expect your usual game, I'll try to smoothen things but in the end you have chosen a Character that doesn't fit neatly and are held responsible for it because you could have done otherwise. Is this understood?&quot;<br /> <br /> To the Umbra models:<br /> Currently I am a bit challenged because I have:<br /> <br /> -a Verbena with a very Gaian bend on Paradigm, Umbra and Magick<br /> <br /> -a non-standard Verbena with Bayonetta as an inspiration (better to say with Bayonetta as an template) including a delusion that leads to all spirits are either angel or demon for her and all Umbrae are either Purgatorio(Penumbra(e)), Paradiso(High Umbra(e)) or Inferno(low Umbra(e))<br /> <br /> -a Solificatus Alchemist (his Paradigm is somewhat malleable/under construction)<br /> <br /> -a Hermetic Dreamwalker (Criamon, inspired by an actual Ars Magica Magus)<br /> <br /> All things stemming from the Umbrae are to be descripted in manifold ways.<br /> <br /> I've already decided, that they can travel together even if they are technically in a region of the Umbrae &quot;impossible&quot; or nonexistent for some members of the cabal.<br /> Each PC has its own lens through which the Umbra gets filtered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034112#post1034112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]<br /> And yet, werewolf players deal with WtA as the Gaia's holy words, and anyone that disagrees is an heretic in the eyes of their Goddess</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that this is a very magey stance. Many Mages are very convinced, that their way is the right/true/only way...<br /> <br /> I recommend to stay polite if you do not intend to start a Flamewar. Your opinion is yours, of course. But the way you worded it is neither respectful nor is it furthering the discussion.<br /> You are free to start a thread with a fitting theme to walz over the Big Fury stubborn and oh so false thinking.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing your opinion.<br /> I hope all other readers, do not read the worst in your post, but take it with a bit of salt (so to speak)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 01-18-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:43:30-08:00","id":1034218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034112#post1034112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I've always felt about WtA &quot;entusiasthics&quot;, and the disciples of the cult of the Wolf always bothered me for being like that... They believe their precious game is the best work of fiction ever, and that their game is the most genious thing ever made since the fire, and all the rest are second class citizens unworth of note, and dare you not to defy their holy scripture that contains all the universal truths written in stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey dude, guess what? My group used Vamprie and Mage as bludgeons to belittle me for liking Werewolf instead of them. The patronizing and insulting attitudes of people online further soured me on Vampire and Mage, and later Demon. Mage isn't a neutral game; it says a lot of things on its own, however odd they are for people that don't experience a click of interest in Mage, and its point of view is one of the many dissonant notes of the WoD cluster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell me, why would any Garou be seduced by the Wyrm, unless he is ignorant about the Garou society or mad? Only an idiot would do that. In fact, &quot;seduction by Wyrm&quot; is not even a theme i wta. </div> </div> </div>Despair and doubt. The contamination is eating everything and the fight looks lost. Some people want to be on the winning side, others eat bullets, others wait to die. Some might not think that everything is going to die all at once, and want to enjoy the ride down. You know, human misconceptions that anything related to humans can have, especially since their bedrock is a visceral feeling and they're part of a massive cosmic being that doesn't often talk to beings as small as they are, if at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is a black spiral dancer &quot;of the wyrm&quot;? Simple: he were born by the wrong parents. Why the other Garou are Champions of Gaia? Simple, they had the RIGHT parents. </div> </div> </div>Not really. To be a member of the BSDs, you actually have to enter the Spiral Labyrinth dance. You might as well apply this line of reasoning to widderslaintes, especially since they can't even do the least little thing to change their lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, in Mage, there is a very real promisse of power. Power for a werewolf isn't that important after all. </div> </div> </div>Did you never read about the Shadow Lords? Or any one person that doesn't want to be pushed around anymore and just wants to be on top and in charge? The temptation is still there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .. What would a Garou aspire for?<br /> <br /> Rank 5? Leadership of a Pack, or a Caern? Well, those are social stances, and doesn't leave much room for alien ancients to make Machiavellian agreements for REAL power to the individual that are one of the essences of the Nefandi Descent. Shifters don't have the inner struggle that endangers their very sense of the self, </div> </div> </div>They have an inner struggle that's not wholly mechanically defined and substantially fuzzier. It makes violence really easy, but violence complicates and escalates. It's similar to how, in Exalted, you can just crush your enemies left and right, but it's going to breed enemies and a cycle of revenge. One of the major points emphasized is that just because changers have jobs to do doesn't mean that the jobs are actually simple to fulfill in execution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet, werewolf players deal with WtA as the Gaia's holy words, and anyone that disagrees is an heretic in the eyes of their Goddess </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> We were talking about cosmology. There are definite differences in what the books say, and the people who worked on them are down as saying that it's set up to be as difficult to make slide together as they could possibly make it. I came here telling people that they aren't reconcilable, someone disagreed and said that they totally were if you used Mage, and then it goes back to the point about how that's proving the point since that's not really a reconciling so much as just applying Mage's viewpoint, and, again, that the way Mage works things isn't actually a neutral setup or middle ground.<br /> <br /> So where does your rant figure into this, again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:45:30-08:00","id":1034254,"title":"","content":"I don't care what game a person likes. And I don't feel offended if people says &quot;hey, Mage sucks. It's a stupid silly game&quot;. But in my personal experience, werewolf players are the most fanatical of all. There is just no subjective truth; there is only the Garou truth, period. That's how wta players are, most of the times. To the point that someone will say &quot;a tomato is a tomato in any place of gaia. It doesn't matter if you are color blind or not, it will always be red and taste sweet&quot;. And many are also saying &quot;Garou are native. <i>Ergo</i> we know our stuff, and could never be wrong. The way is been placed is not just that of &quot;nope, it can't be done. Each to its own&quot;. What has been said so far is &quot;Mages are just a bunch of lunatics, Garou are wise. You lose, I Win&quot;. That's basically it, and upon such approach, sure there can be no middle ground.<br /> <br /> And that has always been my experience with Garou players - it almost seens like the game indoctrination doesnt affect only the PCs, but infects the players themselves. I found my good share of WtA that re","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:49:45-08:00","id":1034260,"title":"","content":"I could even quote such passages in this very thread... Some one literally said that mages are &quot;lunatics&quot; (ergo, everything about Mage is rubbish)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:00:28-08:00","id":1034268,"title":"","content":"Actually, I said that Garou would think that Mages are lunatics because of the subjective nature of Mage Umbra perception. In a mixed group of five Fera and one Mage, the Fera will share the same Umbra perception of a spirit while the Mage will perceive the same spirit differently. When Bastet, Corax, Garou Kitsune, and Mokole agree, but a Mage claims that reality is different than their perception, they are going to think that the Mage is a lunatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:05:17-08:00","id":1034271,"title":"","content":"And for you Saur Spec Ops: I have a little point to disagree.<br /> <br /> Well, basically, for Garou, the High Umbra is just a collective delusion of Mages... It doesn't exist. That's fine by me that the fictional Garou believe that, and it's also fine that this is what some people think too. However, you base your argument in the fact that other games follow the same lines of WtA, and only Mage goes against the tides. That's also fine by me. Well, maybe you're right, who am I to judge. But, I know that when a Vampire uses Auspex 5, when he walks in Astral Form, he is connected to the HIGH UMBRA as per Mage. So, your argument is not so flawless. Sure, it could be one of those many glitches that White Wolf has made over the decades, but still, the Astral Plane is a thing for vampires too, they just don't explore it as much as Mage - well, that place is Mage turf after all.<br /> <br /> Lets be honest - why would vampire games even bother about umbral cosmology? Shaman vampires is a very silly concept (I consider the folklorical werewolf to be turned into a hippie Shaman a silly concept too, but whatever). Mummies, Kuei jin, wraiths... None of those have any business outside the gates of death and the land of the living. Fae folk are in the Dream. Those are all restricted to their neighborhood.<br /> <br /> Who are the real explorers? Mages and shifters. It really is about those two different world views.<br /> <br /> However, like I said, in Vampire the High Umbra is a thing, it's not that important or know for vampires, but it's there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:37:59-08:00","id":1034294,"title":"","content":"No, that is untrue, any Garou can get to the Astral Umbra through the Dream Zone. The Garou are quite aware of the Astral Umbra, their Rage just prevents them from doing much exploring. The Astral Umbra is psychoactive and reacts to the Rage of the Garou negatively. Of course, other Fera (Ananasi, Corax, Mokole, Nuwisha, etc) have fewer problems because they either have no Rage or have different relationships with the Astral Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:58:50-08:00","id":1034395,"title":"","content":"Ok, so here's what I'm getting so far.<br /> <br /> The main differences between WTA and MTA regarding umbra is that of perspective.<br /> <br /> Mage suggests that Spirit world is flexible, bending around the expectations of the observer. The answer changes based on the question.<br /> Werewolf demands that the spirit world be more rigid, that it changes only by the will of the spirits, not the observer. There is a definite single answer, but you must ask the right question.<br /> <br /> For the most part this isn't really a problem since WTA rarely deals with the Lower umbra, Higher umbra or the Dreaming (ignoring Chimera for a moment). Meaning such a rigid view of a spirit world, void of any need of subjectivity isn't really a problem.<br /> But when it comes to the Middle Umbra or the Deep Umbra, this is where things get confusing because both Werewolves and Mages can end up in space.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I can understand your reasoning that any attempt to amalgamate the two is already taking the assumption that Mage is right, because Werewolf explicitly states that the cosmology acts this way independent of any other factors, there need no observer for Gaia to do what she does and Luna to keep that moon going or the Weaver to have the world encased in a web. To say &quot;Well, that's just was Werewolves think is going on&quot; already assumes a subjective pretext to reality.<br /> <br /> So let's look at this the other way. what if both sources are right, but also wrong?<br /> What if Gaia is real, the umbra is part of her domain, and all forms of magic are the shadows of power offered through the trinity of Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld?<br /> What if the Mage's avatar is but a wanton shard of the Umbra itself, one that has fallen free from the confines of its making, and is attracted to human minds, for whom they follow.<br /> <br /> Let's say that Mages are similar to Drones, Fomori, Gorgons, and Kami in that they are humans that have been possessed by a spiritual shard of the umbra. But unlike these four, the spirit is disembodied from Gaia, the Wyrm, Weaver, or Wyld. Perhaps the spirit has even lost all sense of self and purpose, floating raggedly along the umbral storms, flung out into the world of the mundane, forever to flail lost from its intended purpose. This time flailing about changes the spirit into something more subtle, its powers weakening, and its influence breaking, until it returns to its base mode. Gaia spirits to the Questing archetype, Wyld to Dynamic, Weaver to Static, and Wyrm to Primordial. These spirits, if they can even be considered spirits anymore, have been battered and beaten like rocks in a rock tumbler, losing their original form and function, any memories of the war, any affiliation to a side, they are weak and useless lumps of lost potential. And so they clings to humanity in order to survive.<br /> <br /> This spirit now stays attached to this human, feeding of its emotions, its views, its hopes and desires, on its thoughts, dreams, and even its beliefs. Throughout the human's childhood the spirit becomes as much a part of them as anything else the mage thinks. This process shapes them, transforms them, morphs them into aspects of their subconcious, becoming so ingrained in the child that they inhabit that they become more mundane than spirit, they become the avatar, and thus construct a completely new identity built of the imagination and experience of the children they inhabit.<br /> <br /> This transformation, however, leads to quite miraculous things for the avatar, through repeated exposure to the will of humankind, they are able to embody parts of human will to regain a power long lost to them, a power to manipulate the world around them, to change it, to break it, to fix it. This power however, is only accessible via their human's will, meaning they can only act on this power if their human wills it to be. But as more and more humans gain these avatars, the world starts to fluctuate more and more. Consensus starts to emerge, if only a slight amount. The rules of reality become self perpetuating. Unbeknown to these avatar, they are creating a new umbral realm, one of will. For a long time, these avatars work along their human's will to extract change around them based on the desires and thought consumed since infancy. They have only their base essence to motivate them, as well as the memories of previous humans they may have clung on to. It's not until a dramatic event, an awakening, that the human becomes aware of their avatar.<br /> <br /> The awakening gives the avatar much greater access to the human's will, and as such is able to create much more potent effects with the aid of their humans ability to focus their will upon the world. The communication between the avatar and their human is as unique as every human mind, These are the first Mage. These early Mage were much more in tune with their avatar spirits than those that came after them, as this was a time when the consensus was still young and easily mutable, but over time, tribes of humans started to give way to pockets of shared belief, and thus pockets of this umbral realm which obeyed different rules. In order for the avatar to continue acting in accordance with its base essence, it had to find a way to cope with this, and so allowed their mage to incorporate aspects of these beliefs into their practices, keeping their mages will strong and focused so the avatar may continue to function and shape the world as it is want to do.<br /> <br /> Over time, the consensus continued to diversify, and this new umbral realm expanded to encompass the entire world. These avatars became so adhered to their mages, that they ceased being spirits in the traditional sense all together. The possessed no Airte Sense, no ability to communicate via a shared language of the spirits, they had become the very embodiment of human belief, and their only driving force was the base essence they carried, a far cry from the beings they had once been so very long ago.<br /> <br /> Over the centuries many things came and went. The Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld did their best to court these bizarre new &quot;spirits&quot; and in so doing created the seeds for the four factions of the Ascension War. In time the Gauntlet was erected, which created a definitive point of separation between the mundane and the umbral. Perhaps this was a way of controlling this consensual umbral realm lest it infected the rest of Gaia's domain, perhaps it was a direct result of consensual reality when enough humans agreed there was only one world. More likely it was a little of both.<br /> <br /> Centuries pass, and consensual reality has become the mundane world good and proper, with layer upon layer of belief pressed upon them from the humans and their little &quot;spirit&quot; avatars which feed on such belief to enact change. The avatar is no longer a part of the world of the umbra anymore than a Wraith is a part of the skinlands. They are both but fragments of the entities they were before, and have since fallen away.<br /> <br /> When a Mage enters the Spiritual Realm, their avatar acts just as it did before upon its Mage's will, but now it is unhampered by the stifling consensus it had been stuck in prior. Like training in +10G gravity, their avatar found even greater freedom enact their Mage's will, and thus wherever the mage stood created a tiny pocket of consensual reality, adhering to exactly what they expect to see, but as with everything their avatar created, it was no less real.<br /> <br /> The more mages that enter the Spiritual Realm, the more they change it a shape it in their own image, creating lasting changes that may lead to irreversible damage.<br /> <br /> When a human dies, it leaves behind three things (aside from a body). First is its avatar, which will simply tumble around and either find its way to another human, or break down into the building blocks of spiritual energy. Second is the spirit of the human, the compilation of its hopes, dreams, thoughts, and such, which make their home in a shared world of the Astral Umbra. A place where mental energy just feels drawn to. Lastly, they leave behind their Will. The concentrated essence of their desires, passions, regrets, and fears. If the will is strong and filled with such energies, then from this come the Wraith.<br /> <br /> There you go. Mages existing in the WTA universe complete with Consensus defining Avatars. The Paradigms of the various mages are all vastly different descriptions of the functions of the Umbra, the Spirit world, and the trinity of Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld. As the Avatar shifts its role based on the mage it inhabits, such differences are never disprovable. And indeed, it is the effect of their Avatars to shift will around them, that were they to ever come face to face with a Celestine, there is a chance that their sheer belief would transform them into something more palatable for the mage.<br /> <br /> If Gaia were ever to disappear, and the apocalypse were to happen. Then it would happen, but the humans would only see it through their filtered eyes.<br /> <br /> So in a weird way. Mages are to Werewolves what Marauders are to Mages. But in a world were consensus is king, does knowing the &quot;real&quot; truth really mean anything? What good is knowing true colour in the valley of the blind?<br /> <br /> This is reality now. The Umbral shadow of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, there you have it. An interpretation of Mage and Werewolf cosmology that contradicts things from both Mage and Werewolf. The idea is that both the Mage interpretation of reality and the Werewolf interpretation are correct, but at the same time have huge gaps and simplified areas of aspects of what is going on so each side can understand it better. No one actually knows the whole truth, but neither side could have the insight required to understand any of this.<br /> <br /> I probably just created a bit of lore that both WTA and MTA players can hate. So at least they'll agree on something now.<br /> <br /> But yeah. In closing. In the umbra, Everything is Werewolf until a Mage shows up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-18-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:01:25-08:00","id":1034763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray