T12:14:32-08:00","id":1034770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034395#post1034395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so here's what I'm getting so far.<br /> <br /> The main differences between WTA and MTA regarding umbra is that of perspective.<br /> <br /> Mage suggests that Spirit world is flexible, bending around the expectations of the observer. The answer changes based on the question.<br /> Werewolf demands that the spirit world be more rigid, that it changes only by the will of the spirits, not the observer. There is a definite single answer, but you must ask the right question.<br /> <br /> For the most part this isn't really a problem since WTA rarely deals with the Lower umbra, Higher umbra or the Dreaming (ignoring Chimera for a moment). Meaning such a rigid view of a spirit world, void of any need of subjectivity isn't really a problem.<br /> But when it comes to the Middle Umbra or the Deep Umbra, this is where things get confusing because both Werewolves and Mages can end up in space.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I can understand your reasoning that any attempt to amalgamate the two is already taking the assumption that Mage is right, because Werewolf explicitly states that the cosmology acts this way independent of any other factors, there need no observer for Gaia to do what she does and Luna to keep that moon going or the Weaver to have the world encased in a web. To say &amp;quot;Well, that's just was Werewolves think is going on&amp;quot; already assumes a subjective pretext to reality.<br /> <br /> So let's look at this the other way. what if both sources are right, but also wrong?<br /> What if Gaia is real, the umbra is part of her domain, and all forms of magic are the shadows of power offered through the trinity of Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld?<br /> What if the Mage's avatar is but a wanton shard of the Umbra itself, one that has fallen free from the confines of its making, and is attracted to human minds, for whom they follow.<br /> <br /> Let's say that Mages are similar to Drones, Fomori, Gorgons, and Kami in that they are humans that have been possessed by a spiritual shard of the umbra. But unlike these four, the spirit is disembodied from Gaia, the Wyrm, Weaver, or Wyld. Perhaps the spirit has even lost all sense of self and purpose, floating raggedly along the umbral storms, flung out into the world of the mundane, forever to flail lost from its intended purpose. This time flailing about changes the spirit into something more subtle, its powers weakening, and its influence breaking, until it returns to its base mode. Gaia spirits to the Questing archetype, Wyld to Dynamic, Weaver to Static, and Wyrm to Primordial. These spirits, if they can even be considered spirits anymore, have been battered and beaten like rocks in a rock tumbler, losing their original form and function, any memories of the war, any affiliation to a side, they are weak and useless lumps of lost potential. And so they clings to humanity in order to survive.<br /> <br /> This spirit now stays attached to this human, feeding of its emotions, its views, its hopes and desires, on its thoughts, dreams, and even its beliefs. Throughout the human's childhood the spirit becomes as much a part of them as anything else the mage thinks. This process shapes them, transforms them, morphs them into aspects of their subconcious, becoming so ingrained in the child that they inhabit that they become more mundane than spirit, they become the avatar, and thus construct a completely new identity built of the imagination and experience of the children they inhabit.<br /> <br /> This transformation, however, leads to quite miraculous things for the avatar, through repeated exposure to the will of humankind, they are able to embody parts of human will to regain a power long lost to them, a power to manipulate the world around them, to change it, to break it, to fix it. This power however, is only accessible via their human's will, meaning they can only act on this power if their human wills it to be. But as more and more humans gain these avatars, the world starts to fluctuate more and more. Consensus starts to emerge, if only a slight amount. The rules of reality become self perpetuating. Unbeknown to these avatar, they are creating a new umbral realm, one of will. For a long time, these avatars work along their human's will to extract change around them based on the desires and thought consumed since infancy. They have only their base essence to motivate them, as well as the memories of previous humans they may have clung on to. It's not until a dramatic event, an awakening, that the human becomes aware of their avatar.<br /> <br /> The awakening gives the avatar much greater access to the human's will, and as such is able to create much more potent effects with the aid of their humans ability to focus their will upon the world. The communication between the avatar and their human is as unique as every human mind, These are the first Mage. These early Mage were much more in tune with their avatar spirits than those that came after them, as this was a time when the consensus was still young and easily mutable, but over time, tribes of humans started to give way to pockets of shared belief, and thus pockets of this umbral realm which obeyed different rules. In order for the avatar to continue acting in accordance with its base essence, it had to find a way to cope with this, and so allowed their mage to incorporate aspects of these beliefs into their practices, keeping their mages will strong and focused so the avatar may continue to function and shape the world as it is want to do.<br /> <br /> Over time, the consensus continued to diversify, and this new umbral realm expanded to encompass the entire world. These avatars became so adhered to their mages, that they ceased being spirits in the traditional sense all together. The possessed no Airte Sense, no ability to communicate via a shared language of the spirits, they had become the very embodiment of human belief, and their only driving force was the base essence they carried, a far cry from the beings they had once been so very long ago.<br /> <br /> Over the centuries many things came and went. The Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld did their best to court these bizarre new &amp;quot;spirits&amp;quot; and in so doing created the seeds for the four factions of the Ascension War. In time the Gauntlet was erected, which created a definitive point of separation between the mundane and the umbral. Perhaps this was a way of controlling this consensual umbral realm lest it infected the rest of Gaia's domain, perhaps it was a direct result of consensual reality when enough humans agreed there was only one world. More likely it was a little of both.<br /> <br /> Centuries pass, and consensual reality has become the mundane world good and proper, with layer upon layer of belief pressed upon them from the humans and their little &amp;quot;spirit&amp;quot; avatars which feed on such belief to enact change. The avatar is no longer a part of the world of the umbra anymore than a Wraith is a part of the skinlands. They are both but fragments of the entities they were before, and have since fallen away.<br /> <br /> When a Mage enters the Spiritual Realm, their avatar acts just as it did before upon its Mage's will, but now it is unhampered by the stifling consensus it had been stuck in prior. Like training in +10G gravity, their avatar found even greater freedom enact their Mage's will, and thus wherever the mage stood created a tiny pocket of consensual reality, adhering to exactly what they expect to see, but as with everything their avatar created, it was no less real.<br /> <br /> The more mages that enter the Spiritual Realm, the more they change it a shape it in their own image, creating lasting changes that may lead to irreversible damage.<br /> <br /> When a human dies, it leaves behind three things (aside from a body). First is its avatar, which will simply tumble around and either find its way to another human, or break down into the building blocks of spiritual energy. Second is the spirit of the human, the compilation of its hopes, dreams, thoughts, and such, which make their home in a shared world of the Astral Umbra. A place where mental energy just feels drawn to. Lastly, they leave behind their Will. The concentrated essence of their desires, passions, regrets, and fears. If the will is strong and filled with such energies, then from this come the Wraith.<br /> <br /> There you go. Mages existing in the WTA universe complete with Consensus defining Avatars. The Paradigms of the various mages are all vastly different descriptions of the functions of the Umbra, the Spirit world, and the trinity of Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld. As the Avatar shifts its role based on the mage it inhabits, such differences are never disprovable. And indeed, it is the effect of their Avatars to shift will around them, that were they to ever come face to face with a Celestine, there is a chance that their sheer belief would transform them into something more palatable for the mage.<br /> <br /> If Gaia were ever to disappear, and the apocalypse were to happen. Then it would happen, but the humans would only see it through their filtered eyes.<br /> <br /> So in a weird way. Mages are to Werewolves what Marauders are to Mages. But in a world were consensus is king, does knowing the &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; truth really mean anything? What good is knowing true colour in the valley of the blind?<br /> <br /> This is reality now. The Umbral shadow of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, there you have it. An interpretation of Mage and Werewolf cosmology that contradicts things from both Mage and Werewolf. The idea is that both the Mage interpretation of reality and the Werewolf interpretation are correct, but at the same time have huge gaps and simplified areas of aspects of what is going on so each side can understand it better. No one actually knows the whole truth, but neither side could have the insight required to understand any of this.<br /> <br /> I probably just created a bit of lore that both WTA and MTA players can hate. So at least they'll agree on something now.<br /> <br /> But yeah. In closing. In the umbra, Everything is Werewolf until a Mage shows up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that concept... It's a cool myth for creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:54:24-08:00","id":1034796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034763#post1034763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Little quibble here. That whole &quot;Vampire Astral is the High Umbra&quot; thing gets thrown around a lot but it isn't actually explicitly true. Its as much an artifact of headcanon as most other crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say V20 actually clarified it to say that it is the Astral Plane proper (relative to the other lines). When I get home, I can look it up and post a citation. I looked it up relatively recently because of the various discussion on these forums (it's come up 2 or 3 times recently).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034763#post1034763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, speaking as someone else with a less than sanguine view of Werewolf, maybe cool it a little with the game bashing and the implied insults of its fans. Criticism of aspects of the game you don't care for is one thing, but your tone makes it far more condescending and abrasive than it really needs to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a>, that is an interesting compromise between the lines. I don't know that it would satisfy the hardcore fans of either line, but it was an interesting read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:42:17-08:00","id":1034841,"title":"","content":"Actually, the new W20 Umbra book specifically says that astrally projecting Kindred exist in the Astral Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:43:12-08:00","id":1034939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034841#post1034841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the new W20 Umbra book specifically says that astrally projecting Kindred exist in the Astral Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I knew it was said somewhere as of 20th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:46:21-08:00","id":1035039,"title":"","content":"I also know that the W20 Umbra book says basically to the effect of, &quot;Fera are wary of crossing paths with Mages in the Astral Umbra, because the normal forces keeping the latter from going 'all out' are missing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't recall exactly, it's been a while since I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:53:40-08:00","id":1035043,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Astral Umbra is Mage territory, only the Astral Spirits can really face them there. The Archangels will occasionally squish a particularly obnoxious Mage from my understanding, but the Fera should probably not depend on them for help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:17:08-08:00","id":1035206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034271#post1034271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets be honest - why would vampire games even bother about umbral cosmology? Shaman vampires is a very silly concept (I consider the folklorical werewolf to be turned into a hippie Shaman a silly concept too, but whatever). Mummies, Kuei jin, wraiths... None of those have any business outside the gates of death and the land of the living. Fae folk are in the Dream. Those are all restricted to their neighborhood.</div> </div> </div> </div> Putting aside the anecdotal bashing of Werewolf players earlier, one's desire to explore the Umbra depends on the game. And I take issue with the statement that a shaman vampire is silly. Vampire has many wide reaching concepts. Setites, for one, touch on mysticism heavily in this regard, both in their lore and their practice of Setite Sorcery. And various practices of Thaumaturgy/Necromancy touch on related aspects. Spirit Manipulation and Auspex being the top two ways for them to influence it. But as for the why, could be chasing a Werewolf. Working with Werewolves. Perhaps they are hunting for a particular spirit to create a fetish. Maybe they want to find a mage (to make a Blood Mage, Elder seeking a powerful ally, perhaps they want to escape Earth to Horizon. Maybe they work for Pentex. Maybe they want to establish a fortress in the Umbra. Consider the True Black Hand have a city in the Underworld, seems like a good plan. The Tremere do have a ritual that allows them to step into the Umbra fully.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:58:05-08:00","id":1035314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035206#post1035206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Putting aside the anecdotal bashing of Werewolf players earlier, one's desire to explore the Umbra depends on the game. And I take issue with the statement that a shaman vampire is silly. Vampire has many wide reaching concepts. Setites, for one, touch on mysticism heavily in this regard, both in their lore and their practice of Setite Sorcery. And various practices of Thaumaturgy/Necromancy touch on related aspects. Spirit Manipulation and Auspex being the top two ways for them to influence it. But as for the why, could be chasing a Werewolf. Working with Werewolves. Perhaps they are hunting for a particular spirit to create a fetish. Maybe they want to find a mage (to make a Blood Mage, Elder seeking a powerful ally, perhaps they want to escape Earth to Horizon. Maybe they work for Pentex. Maybe they want to establish a fortress in the Umbra. Consider the True Black Hand have a city in the Underworld, seems like a good plan. The Tremere do have a ritual that allows them to step into the Umbra fully.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically, vampires could mess with the Umbra on crossovers, with a few exceptions. That was my point anyway. It's not the focus of the game.<br /> <br /> Hey, you could make a Mage (or some other thing) throw a wraith in the Astral Umbra, but that doesn't mean that the lords of Stygia worry too much about Umbral Lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:29:03-08:00","id":1035331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035314#post1035314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically, vampires could mess with the Umbra on crossovers, with a few exceptions. That was my point anyway. It's not the focus of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or any game with a Vampire with Auspex 5. Or a few of the less common powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:38:40-08:00","id":1035338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035314#post1035314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, basically, vampires could mess with the Umbra on crossovers, with a few exceptions. That was my point anyway. It's not the focus of the game.<br /> <br /> Hey, you could make a Mage (or some other thing) throw a wraith in the Astral Umbra, but that doesn't mean that the lords of Stygia worry too much about Umbral Lore</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's certainly not what you had said. Your statement was, 'why would vampire games even bother about umbral cosmology?' Games, not THE GAME. And there are plenty of good hooks for Vampires to want to deal/explore Umbral cosmology, as I said. It matters if you want to deal with Auspex 5 anymore than spying, various uses of Thaumaturgy (or related Blood Sorcery schools that interact with spirits), Koldunism, and arguably Abyss Mysticism. Someone asked just the other day (I think in the Werewolf forum) about where Kupala (a super powerful demonic entity in Vampire) would fall in a Werewolf crossover. And there was some contention. Obviously Kupala should be extremely powerful within Vampire. But within Werewolf, maybe thought it was perhaps a middling entity. Heck, arguably even the existence of the Triat versus God and Caine can be an awkward question to answer, yet relates to what the universe is. How it is structured.<br /> <br /> The entire aspect of Koldunism is commanding spirits. You kind of have to figure out how that actually works in a crossover with such ease when it goes different for Mages/Werewolves. And where they come from. Where does the Abyss fall in with everything else? Descriptions vary greatly and matters a lot for some of the uses of it. So on and so forth. As far as the High Umbra existing in Vampire, the core book at least describes it as a place with ghosts, shades, werewolves, and magi. That itself seems to conflict with the supposed Garou/Mage disagreement on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 01-20-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:15:22-08:00","id":1035369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> s far as the High Umbra existing in Vampire, the core book at least describes it as a place with ghosts, shades, werewolves, and magi. That itself seems to conflict with the supposed Garou/Mage disagreement on it. </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah. That line made me think that vampires traveled to a sort of &quot;universal penumbra&quot; of their own.<br /> I'm intrigued of what W20 book of the Umbra has to say about this (have to read the book), although I think there will never be an official consensus of this things. <br /> Crossover stuff always needs to be decided in-game. Perhaps it's for the better, as you can tie the cosmology to your play. Need vampires in the Dark Umbra?, well, that's where they go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:26:48-08:00","id":1035377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1034111#post1034111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you use Werewolf books. There are strong distinctions between the Three Umbrae, perhaps more than in Mage, as there's no interrelated Videres sharing a Penumbral landscape.<br /> <br /> Mages are reality warpers that reshape reality like they were powerful spirits (Paradigms are mere delusions). They may be an abomination to Gaia (or perhaps this it's a werewolf prejudice, it wouldn't be the first).<br /> <br /> Mages may not be able to go wherever werewolves go, but not because their perception of reality doesn't encompass that particular Umbral manifestation, but because they're forbidden by the spirits to go to that place, or because they lack the powers needed to travel there. A subtle but powerful difference, that may impede your Gaian Dreamspeaker from going to garou sacred lands, despite being paradigmatically OK for him.<br /> <br /> Certain places where mages go might not exist, or maybe they exist but are interpreted in a &amp;quot;werewolf way&amp;quot;. This may be as simple or as hard as you want.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers can now explore very far in conventional space, indeed, now that material space encompases all the universe. They should be very happy with this, as they're not inventing the void and setting the laws of physics while they travel, they were already set from the begining-this it's a stronger confirmation of a scientific world than the Antrophic Principle. Too bad that they're unwitting pawns of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could the Mage simply being &quot;creating reality&quot; as he walks on the Umbra to fit what he expect to see? (Or been just having allucinations...)<br /> <br /> Well... In a Werewolf game, you could just say that when mages try to go outside the Deep Umbra, they just go to Maia, or maybe to the Deep Dreaming perhaps... That would be interesting... And make a huge change...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:33:13-08:00","id":1035418,"title":"","content":"Not the Deep Dreaming. Mages lose access to True Magick when they enter the Deep Dreaming and go insane from what I remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:11:00-08:00","id":1035443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035418#post1035418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the Deep Dreaming. Mages lose access to True Magick when they enter the Deep Dreaming and go insane from what I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every once in a while I feel like I can see the seams. Mage was written with the astral and primal planes in mind, so it has rules for them. The underworld and dreaming were defined after mage 1e, so mages have a harder time surviving them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:31:17-08:00","id":1035509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035418#post1035418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the Deep Dreaming. Mages lose access to True Magick when they enter the Deep Dreaming and go insane from what I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, maybe they could get stuck at the gates of Arcadia, or in Mid Dream, or in Maia (or Maya, I don't know the world in english, the representation of the land of dreams in the Middle Umbra), something like that... Could that sort of thing be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:20:55-08:00","id":1035568,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t know that there was an \u201coutside\u201d of the Deep Umbra (well, appart from the &quot;closer&quot; umbras). Always assumed it was \u201cthe final frontier \u201c, even for Werewolf. What it\u2019s supposed to be outside of the Deep Umbra?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:22:30-08:00","id":1035569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030886-reaching-the-deep-umbra?p=1035568#post1035568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn\u2019t know that there was an \u201coutside\u201d of the Deep Umbra (well, appart from the &amp;quot;closer&amp;quot; umbras). Always assumed it was \u201cthe final frontier \u201c, even for Werewolf. What it\u2019s supposed to be outside of the Deep Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that man was not meant to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T18:22:45-08:00","id":1035570,"title":"","content":"Nothing? The Deep Umbra extends to infinity in every possible direction as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T22:12:35-08:00","id":1035625,"title":"","content":"There was an interesting quote regarding the Deep Umbra in M20 under the header 'Return to the Inner Experience':<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supposedly, deep space leads back into the<br /> Earthly realm. I\u2019ve heard that Umbral travelers<br /> occasionally wind up in the blackest regions of<br /> our oceans and that deep sea travelers discover<br /> portals into space. Once again, recursive<br /> quirks in the universe connect \u201cout there\u201d<br /> with \u201cin here.\u201d Perhaps, as the Masters of<br /> Correspondence say, all places really are one<br /> place. The distance between them is merely<br /> an illusion we can transcend if and when we<br /> learn to forget everything we think we know. </div> </div> </div>Written from a subjective standpoint, but it's once again an interesting twist of Mage theme and philosophy on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T22:19:41-08:00","id":1035630,"title":"","content":"It could be that Mages are more anchored than Garou and their Avatars force them to return if they go too far out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T23:21:31-08:00","id":1035634,"title":"","content":"Don't confuse finding paths from the outermost to the innermost with being forced back.<br /> Also, it wouldn't explain how it also works the other way around. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Either way, it shows another alien quirk of the Umbrascape that might be different between gamelines. The Umbra *is* infinite in Mage as well. And that's without even going into things like the the Shade Realms possibly opening up into parallel whole universes of an alien nature. (One theory is that the whole Universe of the WoD is actually the inside of the S.R. of the tenth sphere, hence why it cannot be found.). Heck, it's pretty much semi-confirmed in the case of S.R. Matter, which is a revese of the universe in terms of space and matter from what they've found so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}